  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">IN THEODORI BEZÆ</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="1">A'ξρaʓυσίαν A Io. Iacomoto versibus</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="1">elegantissimis expositam.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>Acmóte, sidi quod generis patrem,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Mandata summi Patris st audiit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Charà litantem protinus hostiâ,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Quòd patre dignam progeniem suo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Ipsam obsequentem protinus hostiam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Sacri tuendam das oculis chori:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Quàm rite factum! quàm bene, commodè,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Quàm congruenter temporibus malis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Contaminatis, prodigialibus!</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Nam quid malorum luxuriantium</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Primas scatebras quaerimus anxij?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Tantùm Vnde terris scilicet exteri,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Ciuilis aeque sanguinis Vndique:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Quis iste gentes immedicabilis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Quis iste Reges exagitet furor:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Aut cur suarum persluat immemor</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Natura legum, aut insiciat lues</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Perennis auras: mortium imagines</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Passim, &amp; reclufis Tartara faucibus:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Et ipsa ruptis, ô scelus, ô pudor,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Iamiam fathiscant iura repagulis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Heu prima labes primáque tristium</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Woodcut initial "A" (decorated) at start of verse; the stanza lines are printed as continuous verse in the scan and are transcribed as one paragraph. Some words are uncertain in the Greek title and in the verse (e.g. "Acmóte", "Vnde") and should be checked against the original.</notes>
